# Data Backup Ignore Configuration
# Gitignore-style patterns for rsync --exclude-from (see docs/backup-principles.md
# for the principles behind every rule and the exact pattern semantics).
#
# Dedicated to the secondary data disk (/data), housing active projects,
# repositories, datasets, and personal data.
#
# Decide per entry: is this data (rarity tiers 1-3 -> keep) or is it
# rebuildable/re-obtainable (tiers 4-5 -> exclude)?

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- tier 5: caches & tmp
lost+found/
.cache/
.thumbnails/
.Trash-*/
tmp/
.tmp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*~

# ------------------------------------------------ tier 4/5: build artifacts & deps
# Unanchored patterns match directories at any depth without needing **/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.dart_tool/
target/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.turbo/
.gradle/caches/
.m2/repository/

# AI tool local model checkpoints or caches (tier 4 - re-downloadable)
.ollama/
models/cache/

# ------------------------------------------------ tier 4: bulk re-obtainable media
*.iso
vms/instances/
vms/images/*.tmp

# ------------------------------------------------ tier 2/3: cold archives (managed via tm archive)
archive/

# ------------------------------------------------ tier 5: unbacked scratchpad & safehouse zones
# Ephemeral scratch spaces, temporary media, or disposable testbeds (never backed up)
scratch/
safehouse/
media/
no-backup/
